MicroSim: CORS Blockage Visualization MicroSim: CORS Blockage Visualization - Title: Browser Security vs Local Audio - Description: An interactive diagram showing an HTTP request for an <code>.mp3</code> file. When the user tries to load it via <code>file:///</code>, a large red shield blocks the request, illustrating the CORS security constraints. When the user toggles on the Python server, the shield turns green and the audio file successfully loads into the p5.js sketch. <p>Here is an example of setting up your HTML file to load p5.js locally. Notice how we must structure our files explicitly, unlike the automatic web editor.</p> <pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;meta charset="UTF-8"&gt;
  &lt;title&gt;Local p5.js Project&lt;/title&gt;
  &lt;!-- Load the library locally or via CDN --&gt;
  &lt;script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/p5.js/1.9.0/p5.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
  &lt;!-- Load accessibility features --&gt;
  &lt;script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/p5.js/1.9.0/addons/p5.sound.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
  &lt;script src="sketch.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;main&gt;
    &lt;!-- Canvas will be dynamically injected here --&gt;
  &lt;/main&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
</code></pre>
